# Process 3.4, the body of portal.router.ServeHTTP: the portal handler's
# answer to each request that box 9.4 sends it. The response writer of the
# request passes unchanged from box 9.4 to box 3.4.3. Each box reads the
# router's sites, access hook and routes as its receiver.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number --number-prefix 3.4. docs/flow.3.4.dfd -o flow.3.4.svg

{9.4 Answer each request with the portal handler of the snapshot in service}
> request
[3.4.1. Ask the access hook for the access of the request's reader, once: Everything without a hook, and an access that allows nothing after an error or a nil access, whose cause goes to the log
 (portal.router.readerAccess)]
    > request
    < access, error
    <Embedding program>
    > hook problem
    <Log>
> access
[3.4.2. Build the reader's view: the access and the reader's sites, a copy of the site of each visible portal with only its visible sections
 so that every page of the request reads only what is visible to the reader
 (portal.router.viewFor)]
    > portal, section
    < allowed
    <Embedding program>
> response writer, request, view
[3.4.3. Send the request with the reader's view through the routes to its page, and with an access hook write the response with Cache-Control: private
 (portal.router.route)]
    > file path
    < file
    <Documentation root>
    > toc problem
    <Log>
    > response
    <HTTP server>

# type: request = *net/http.Request
# type: access = portal.Access
# type: error = error
# type: hook problem = error
# type: portal = portal.Portal
# type: section = portal.Section
# type: allowed = bool
# type: response writer = net/http.ResponseWriter
# type: view = *portal.view
# type: file path = string
# type: file = []byte
# type: toc problem = error
# type: response = []byte
